🗣
"Face Talk"/en
===
¶Your facial expressions, tracked by camera and narrated on stage.¶

¶ Make a face stream to track expressions ¶
face: Face(200ms)

¶ Decide between smiling, frowing, blinking, or nothing ¶
mood: face.eyesOpen ?
		(face.smileAmount > 0.6 ? 'smiling'
			face.frownAmount > 0.4 ? 'frowning'
				'')
	'blinking'

¶ Convert the mood to an emoji, and give the face a speech bubble saying it.
Giving the bubble a @Say means the mood is spoken aloud as well as shown, and
the bubble stands in for the caption at the foot of the stage. ¶
Stage([
		Phrase(
			(mood = 'blinking' ? '😴'
				mood = 'smiling' ? '😀'
					mood = 'frowning' ? '🙁'
						'😐')
			size: 8m
			bubble: (mood = ''
				? Bubble(`/Smile, frown, or close your eyes/` wrap: 8m)
				Bubble(Say(mood)))
		)
	])
